\ ---- format (Iteration 781) -----------------------------------------------
\ format(f, a, b, ...): Python's % formatting - the conversions s d i f x X
\ and %%, the flags - 0 + and space, a width and a precision. The text is
\ built in a block of the C heap kept from call to call, then made a text.
\ f rounds half away from zero on Rill's exact decimals (Python rounds the
\ binary float's value: the two differ only on an exact tie).
VARIABLE FM-B  VARIABLE FM-N  VARIABLE FM-CAP  VARIABLE FM-C
: FM-ROOM ( u --- )   \ room for u more bytes
  FM-N @ + DUP FM-CAP @ > 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  2* 256 MAX DUP FM-CAP !
  FM-B @ ?DUP IF SWAP RESIZE ELSE ALLOCATE THEN THROW FM-B ! ;
: FM-ADD ( a u --- )   DUP FM-ROOM  TUCK FM-B @ FM-N @ + SWAP MOVE  FM-N +! ;
: FM-CH ( c --- )   FM-C C!  FM-C 1 FM-ADD ;

\ ---- The collector (Iteration 776) ---------------------------------------
\ Rill's values live in the arena, which only grew. At a safe point - between two statements of
\ the script's top level, where no value is held anywhere but in variables - once the arena has
\ grown past R-GC-AT, everything the registered variables reach is copied into a new arena, and
\ the old one is freed back to the system. The copy compacts: a list's items array is cut to its
\ count. The compilers register every variable of the script that can hold a text, a list, a
\ record or an item, and every top-level loop's source, with its kind (R-ROOT); a literal text
\ made once (gene littext) is kept outside the arena (R-FIX), as the regex cache's patterns are.
9 CONSTANT R-ITEM                                     \ an item variable's kind: compile.4's K-ANY
: R-FIX ( t --- t' )   \ a text copied out of the arena, for good
  R-T@ DUP CELL+ ALLOCATE THROW >R  DUP R@ !  R@ CELL+ SWAP MOVE  R> ;
512 CONSTANT G-MAXROOTS
G-MAXROOTS CELLS BUFFER: G-RV   G-MAXROOTS CELLS BUFFER: G-RK   VARIABLE G-RN
: R-ROOT ( addr kind --- )
  G-RN @ G-MAXROOTS < 0= ABORT" rill: too many variables to collect"
  G-RK G-RN @ CELLS + !  G-RV G-RN @ CELLS + !  1 G-RN +! ;
VARIABLE G-OLD  VARIABLE G-END  VARIABLE G-TOP  VARIABLE G-BITS  VARIABLE G-RUNS
: G-IN? ( a --- f )   DUP G-OLD @ U< 0= SWAP G-END @ U< AND ;
: G-BIT ( a --- byte-addr mask )   G-OLD @ - 3 RSHIFT  DUP 3 RSHIFT G-BITS @ +  SWAP 7 AND 1 SWAP LSHIFT ;
: G-FWD? ( a --- f )   G-BIT SWAP C@ AND 0<> ;
: G-ALLOT ( n --- a )   7 + -8 AND  G-TOP @ SWAP OVER + G-TOP ! ;
: G-MOVE ( a n --- a' )   \ an object's n bytes into the new arena; the old place forwarded to it
  DUP G-ALLOT >R  OVER R@ ROT MOVE  R@ OVER !  G-BIT OVER C@ OR SWAP C!  R> ;
DEFER G-COPY ( a kind --- a' )
: G-TEXT ( t --- t' )   DUP G-IN? 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP G-FWD? IF @ EXIT THEN  DUP @ CELL+ G-MOVE ;
: G-BOX ( b --- b' )   \ an item, and what it holds
  DUP G-IN? 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP G-FWD? IF @ EXIT THEN
  DUP @ >R  2 CELLS G-MOVE  R>
  DUP K-TEXT = OVER K-LIST = OR OVER K-REC = OR IF OVER CELL+ @ SWAP G-COPY OVER CELL+ ! ELSE DROP THEN ;
: G-LIST ( l --- l' )   \ a list: its header, its items array cut to the count, each item
  DUP G-IN? 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP G-FWD? IF @ EXIT THEN
  3 CELLS G-MOVE
  DUP @ OVER CELL+ !
  DUP @ CELLS 8 MAX G-ALLOT
  OVER 2 CELLS + @ OVER 3 PICK @ CELLS MOVE  OVER 2 CELLS + !
  DUP @ 0 ?DO  DUP 2 CELLS + @ I CELLS +  DUP @ G-BOX SWAP !  LOOP ;
: G-REC ( r --- r' )   \ a record: its keys and values, and its hash table as it is (indices, no pointers)
  DUP G-IN? 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP G-FWD? IF @ EXIT THEN
  4 CELLS G-MOVE
  DUP @ G-LIST OVER !  DUP CELL+ @ G-LIST OVER CELL+ !
  DUP 2 CELLS + @ IF  DUP 2 CELLS + @  OVER 3 CELLS + @ CELLS  DUP G-ALLOT  DUP >R SWAP MOVE  R> OVER 2 CELLS + !  THEN ;
: G-COPY-IMPL ( a kind --- a' )
  DUP K-TEXT = IF DROP G-TEXT EXIT THEN  DUP K-LIST = IF DROP G-LIST EXIT THEN
  DUP K-REC = IF DROP G-REC EXIT THEN  R-ITEM = IF G-BOX THEN ;
' G-COPY-IMPL IS G-COPY
: R-GC ( --- )   \ what the variables reach, copied to a new arena; the old one freed
  R-ARENA0 @ G-OLD !  R-TOP @ G-END !
  R-ARENA-SIZE ALLOCATE THROW  DUP G-TOP !  >R
  R-TOP @ R-ARENA0 @ - 64 / 1+  DUP ALLOCATE THROW  DUP G-BITS !  SWAP ERASE
  G-RN @ 0 ?DO  G-RV I CELLS + @  DUP @ G-RK I CELLS + @ G-COPY  SWAP !  LOOP
  CWD-STACK @ ?DUP IF G-LIST CWD-STACK ! THEN
  G-BITS @ FREE THROW  R-ARENA0 @ FREE THROW
  R> DUP R-ARENA0 !  R-ARENA-SIZE + R-END !  G-TOP @ R-TOP !
  R-TOP @ R-ARENA0 @ - 2* 16777216 MAX R-TOP @ + R-END @ MIN R-GC-AT !
  G-STRESS @ IF R-TOP @ 65536 + R-GC-AT ! THEN  1 G-RUNS +! ;     \ under stress: again after 64 KB more
: R-GC? ( --- )   R-TOP @ R-GC-AT @ U> IF R-GC THEN ;   \ a safe point: the compilers put one before each top-level statement
\ SIGNALS-PENDING scans every flag (~27 ns): looked at every 1024th safe point, and at the first after each command
: R-GC?S ( --- )   \ a script with on EXIT: a signal caught, then exit 128 + it (786)
  R-GC?  -1 SIG-CNT +!  SIG-CNT @ 0< IF 1023 SIG-CNT !  R-SIGNAL ?DUP IF 128 + R-EXIT THEN THEN ;
